\ Workload for the freeze-time parameter-narrowing A/B, run by
\ `make benchmark-param-inference`.
\
\ This is the Fibonacci repro from the parameter-inference bug with printing
\ removed, so both halves of the A/B build: the locked build narrows
\ `fib-step`'s parameters and the dip-invoked quotation's, and the default build
\ leaves them opaque.
\
\ The bug reported this workload at 5000 repetitions. The narrowing turns out to
\ be worth only a few percent on the loop, so the count is raised until that
\ margin clears run-to-run spread. It lands the loop around a fifth of a second
\ against a spread of a few milliseconds.
\
\ The final comparison guards the measurement. A miscompile that produced a wrong
\ sum would otherwise report a meaningless time.

fib-step: ( a b n -- result ) [
  dup 0 = [ drop drop ] [
    1 - [ swap over + ] dip fib-step
  ] if
] ;

fib: ( n -- n ) [
  dup 2 < [ ] [
    0 1 <rot- fib-step
  ] if
] ;

repeat-fib: ( n -- ) [
  dup 0 = [ drop ] [
    1 - 30 fib drop repeat-fib
  ] if
] ;

100000 repeat-fib

30 fib 832040 = [ ] [ 1 0 / drop ] if
